The conversation focused on crafting a section for a grant proposal addressing the relevance of proposed research on solar radiation management (SRM) to NASA's strategic goals and the EPSCoR mission. James expressed concerns that the initial draft lacked specificity and aimed to incorporate specific NASA strategic objectives, such as understanding Earth's climate system (1.1), ensuring data accessibility (1.3), and advancing transformational space technologies (3.1). I provided an edited version of the proposal that explicitly linked the research activities to these objectives, emphasizing the project's contributions to the scientific community, economic development in Delaware, and interdisciplinary collaboration with relevant institutions and NASA partners. The revised draft highlighted the project's potential to enhance research infrastructure, educate students, and address global sustainability challenges.
